      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Jack (Jackson) Melvus Miser.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 2 as a officer. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>Commander of the Order of Jack; Knight of the Regal Lion</strong> — The Order of Jack (founder and commander) / the Regal Lion (knight, formerly second-in-command) / the Iron Legion (by the Regal Lion's subordination, not by oath)</p><p>Status: Active — minor landed knight-commander at Vellanet Rise; Regal Lion second-in-command on detached service; unaware his brother Archie is missing</p><p>Jack Melvus Miser is the eldest of the five Miser children and the reason the rest of them eat well. A paladin of the Oath of Glory who joined the Regal Lion at fifteen, he ground his way up from squire to the order's second-in-command on bandit cordons, unpriceable monster contracts, and one daylight kill on a rampaging Fire Elemental Myrmidon in front of a whole market town. He now holds Vellanet Rise — a minor Midlands-periphery grant of a fortified manor, three villages, a mill and a quarry — and leads his own body of arms, the Order of Jack, whose famous 20,000 is a muster roll rather than an army. Locally he is a hero; a hundred miles away he is nobody. He lifted his mother Wanda and his siblings out of poverty exactly as he said he would at fifteen, and has not yet been told that the brother missing from the family portrait is wanted across three planes.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Sabre</strong> — “Weapon of choice a Flame-Tongue longsword, rare and openly worn; a shortsword kept for the day the fire is the wrong answer.”</li><li><strong>Leadership</strong> — “Commander of the Order of Jack; Knight of the Regal Lion”</li><li><strong>Iron Discipline</strong> — “The Order of Jack (founder and commander) / the Regal Lion (knight, formerly second-in-command) / the Iron Legion (by the Regal Lion's subordination, not by oath)”</li><li><strong>Loud</strong> — “July lightened the load; he says so himself, loudly, to anyone who calls him self-made.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/jack_melvus_miser</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/jack_melvus_miser</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
